s us 73 centibench score per watt  compared to 400 on the macbook air and  with the macbook air once it starts  throttling down its efficiency actually  goes up a lot i did another video about  low power mode and how fast and cool it  runs another great one to watch i'll  link it at the end now as far as  geekbench the single core score is 73  higher on the macbook air while the  multi-core score is 44 higher on the mac  pro so less of a difference for those  quick snappy tasks even in multi-core as  far as graphics the mac pro is about  four times more powerful in metal  compute tasks that is a massive  difference uh and that's compared to the  eight core the ten core we don't  recommend we tested it out it does  throttle quite a bit and it can't slow  down when you need that extra  performance so the mac pro is a lot more  powerful but what happens for your daily  simple tasks well first off in  speedometer 2.0 the m2air scores two and  a half times more points and it is way  faster for day-to-day browsing when i'm  on my mac pro i notice how everything is  slower it is crazy now not only that we  were compressing files decompressing and  for xcode the m2 air was 20  faster at compressing the application  all those tiny files now when we  decompress that it is actually 45  faster and that's with both using the  same mac os another thing we do all the  time is denoising our audio recordings  for our youtube videos the mac pro took  45 seconds compared to just 26 on the m2  macbook air so that's 42  faster and get this that is using  rosetta because this app is still  written for intel cpus that is crazy so  pretty much every day-to-day simple task  is much snappier with this fanless  laptop but what about tougher tasks  because that's what the mac pro is for  well as far as pure graphics gaming  performance which we don't really game  on it but this thing's really capable  and it was what it came out the mac pro  scored 2.25 times more frames per second  than the m2 macbook air which of course  is fanless and we have the bend graphics  now to do that the mac pro took over 22  times more wattage and power for the  graphics to achieve the fps which means  that the m2 macbook air is way more  efficient of course it gets over 8  frames per second per watt compared to  less than one now of course this thing  is plugged in it's meant to suck a lot  of power for things like blender where  you really need those high performance  graphics and that's exactly what it did  it was over three times faster in our  classroom scene and with that zn  processor being super stable it destroys  in logic pro it can handle a ton of  tracks and with that we also have a ton  of ram capability in here we have  192. you can go up to a terabyte and a  half with higher processors compared to  up to 24 gigabytes on the m2 macbook air  so it is definitely a killer for doing  really high-end stuff now as far as  coding this was very interesting not  only does it sip power but it was  actually faster than this mac pro at our  standard project that you could test out  for yourself as well this is where apple  silicon software optimization really  kicks in because there's no way that the  m2 air should be faster in processing  code but if a application's optimized it  is insanely quick  and moving along into photo editing with  photoshop the m2 also has the neural  engine that can speed stuff up i  processed nine images for hdr and the mt  macbook air was 34  faster now some people do more images or  they have bigger differences or i know  people that do this all day for real  estate photography and it's crazy that  this laptop can replace and beat out a  high-end intel mac desktop that is  insane now check out this next one  running a 10 image panorama where  photoshop does all the processing for  you the m2 air was more than twice as  fast it was insanely quick and it's just  mind-blowing looking at the raw  performance versus actual real world  tasks that people do now when i saw  these photoshop results i was like man  that is incredible what about for  lightroom there's a lot of people that  use it for processing batches of images  and i started testing it out and then my  mind was blown because the mac pro was  flying for example exporting our 50 42  megapixel edited images to jpeg the mac  pro took 1 minute and 11 seconds  previously which was way faster than all  the other intel macs even the imac pros  this thing because of its six channel  memory just flew  way beyond the raw performance now in  2022 the m2 air took one minute and 10  seconds  meaning that it's just insanely faster  than everything else out there but get  this the apple silk and max were not the  only ones that people are optimizing it  for adobe enabled gpu rendering for  images i think they redid the engine and  now this mac pro with this beefy  graphics card did it in 32 seconds so  more than twice as fast and that just  shows that for some people having these  high-end graphics it's still going to  make a big difference especially if  you're doing this all day  for your main job or your business now  apple really focused on the media  engines in the m2 chip and they  surprised us with prores decoding and  encoding so this thing is actually quite  capable for video editing and go ahead  and take a look what happens stabilizing  a one minute 4k clip which we stabilized  all the time was more than twice as fast  as this mac pro and that blows my mind  what the optimizations have done now  exporting a five minute hevc project  with effects was also slightly faster  where the mac pro used to be by far the  quickest now what's crazier is if we use  davinci resolve which recently was  updated for this m2 chip that actually  goes down to a minute and 32 seconds  beating out the macro by a lot now the  mac pro is fully optimized they can't  get any faster but final cut can get  faster with future updates now one thing  that really got to me about the mac pro  once i got it was that newer footage  like 10 bit 422 would not play smoothly  it would just be super choppy because  the system can't handle it now apple  addressed that with their apple silicon  chips which were the first that can play  back smoothly even on a base m1 macbook  air now the m2 builds upon it apple  talked about 8k video and we started to  shoot ak video for our top angle that  way we can zoom in and show you guys all  of the details that are very clear and  it's been great other than the mac pro  not being able to play back these 8k  hevc clips and it's just super choppy  but get this the m2 macbook air plays  them back  perfectly now on the mac pro you have to  transcode this footage into another  format that's easier to play and to do  30 minutes of transcoding it takes 49  minutes that is a long time to wait to  be able to edit these files whereas the  m2 it takes 18 minutes to do the same  exact tasks but of course you don't even  have to do that because it plays back  perfectly now as i mentioned we were  shocked that apple added the prores  decoders and encoders into a base chip  they had that with the pro models and  that was fantastic but now we have it  here so how fast is it with the mac pro  you have the two thousand dollar after  burner card to do this same thing  whereas here we have a whole laptop with  battery display everything else for  sixteen hundred so taking our five  minute prores raw graded project our  macbook air plays it back perfectly and  it rendered it out in a minute and 51  seconds now the mac pro takes two  minutes and 45 seconds without the after  burner card and if you spend that two  grand it goes down to a minute and 45  seconds just slightly faster than the m2  macbook air now as i mentioned  we have the 8 core here now we also have  the 10 core which we tested and for most  things it's not really worth it but for  pro res it actually speeds it up to a  minute and 40 seconds uh meaning it is  faster than the mac pro with that after  burner uh because we are gpu limited in  this instance so that is just so crazy  that for a fanless laptop you could play  this footage better and easier than on  the mac pro it is incredible now there  has to be some areas where the mac pro  is better and there are for example in  davinci resolve if you're denoising  footage this takes all of the raw  graphics power to do in our macbook air  can play this back at only three frames  per second out of 24 whereas the mac pro  it could do it in 18 seconds so still  not perfect so you might want to render  and it'll be way faster render on the  mac pro but a huge difference because of  that raw graphics power now the same  thing goes if you are working with ak  crazy footage the mac pros over three  times faster at doing this compared to  the macbook air and here of course it  starts thermal throttling a lot now i  mentioned that uh cooling fan that we  had with the thermal pads when we use  that on this machine it went down from  26 minutes almost 27 down to 19 minutes  and 40 seconds it was actually faster  than our m2 macbook pro which really  blew our mind so that does make a really  good improvement now overall yes the mac  pro still has its place you have the pci  cards you could do dual graphics cards  you could get a lot of ram  but at this point for the vast majority  people the apple silicon laptops and the  mac mini and the mac studio they make so  much sense that unless you need one of  the small a few small niche features of  the mac pro it is just slower in most  cases and for what most people do so  there you guys go if you guys want to  buy one of these from me please reach  out if you do need the pci slots or  something else i'd be glad to sell it to  you for a good deal and please check out  that  cooling video where we added a fan and  we tested out the laptop cooler on the  m2 macbook air it is amazing click above  to subscribe this been max and i'll see  you in the next video  [Music]  you

